{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791069268,"nonce":"nzQ2VBi3NlXq21Q30BEbZm1HSxE=","title":"align-items: baseline aligns box bottoms, not baselines, for text leaves","message":"taffy 0.6 never receives a first baseline for a text leaf. compute/leaf.rs\nreturns first_baselines: Point::NONE, and a measure function can only\nreturn a Size. compute/flexbox.rs then uses\nfirst_baselines.y.unwrap_or(size.height), so align-items: baseline\naligns the bottom of each box.\n\nBlinc hides this for same-size text by sizing single-line text to\nfont_size * line_height and drawing at top + ascender. Two faces at\ndifferent sizes have different ascenders, so their drawn baselines\ndiverge. Measured in crates/blinc_layout/tests/baseline_alignment.rs:\n16px sans beside 14px monospace with 1px padding diverge by 0.60px under\nthe fallback estimator, more with real faces and a wider size gap.\n\nReported by the ashui session, which renders a 0.9em monospace \"code\"\ninside a 16px sans paragraph and sees it sit visibly high. Tracked there\nas da2832a3fa495de0326fdc4c6132dee87d8c0b341c60c3abe4ead879d3064068.\n\n\nThe suggestion was to compute leaf layout through taffy's low-level API\nand set first_baselines. That is not reachable from outside: the\ndispatch that would carry it is LayoutPartialTree::compute_child_layout\nimplemented on TaffyView, which is pub(crate) and reads private tree\nstate (taffy.nodes, node_context_data, the layout cache). A newtype\nwrapper cannot forward the other trait methods, so there is nothing to\noverride.\n\n\n1. Implement LayoutPartialTree over Blinc's own node storage, replacing\n   TaffyTree. Gives full control, and means reimplementing node\n   storage, the layout cache, traversal and rounding. A rewrite of\n   blinc_layout's core for one alignment mode.\n\n2. Carry a baseline out of the measure function in a patched taffy, and\n   let taffy's flexbox do the alignment it already implements. By far\n   the smallest correct change, and the cost is maintaining a fork of a\n   core layout dependency. Worth attempting upstream first.\n\n3. Align baselines in a Blinc post-layout pass: shift each baseline-\n   aligned item by (line baseline - own baseline offset) and regrow the\n   container. Needs no taffy change, and reimplements a slice of\n   flexbox, including cross-size recomputation, wrapping lines and\n   nesting. Fragile in general even where it works for a simple row.\n\n\nBlinc draws text at top + ascender (blinc_app context.rs). ashui places\nit at top + half_leading + ascender, which is what CSS specifies. So the\ntwo already disagree about where the baseline sits inside the box,\nindependently of taffy. Whichever route is taken, reporting a CSS\nbaseline to taffy while painting without half-leading would misalign\nBlinc's own text. The paint path has to move to half-leading in the same\nchange.\n\n\ncrates/blinc_layout/tests/baseline_alignment.rs states the acceptance\ncriterion from the request as an ignored test, plus two that run: one\nguarding the same-face case that already works, and one asserting that\nbox bottoms coincide today, which will start failing if taffy ever gives\nleaves a baseline. No behaviour changed.","files":null}]}